# Give Excalibur its own identity on Windows so it installs side by side with
# Chromium or ungoogled-chromium instead of sharing their install directory,
# profile (%LOCALAPPDATA%\Excalibur\User Data), registry keys, file
# associations and notification activator.
#
# Not changed yet: the elevation service and tracing service CLSIDs/IIDs, which
# must be changed together with their IDL files. They only matter for
# system-level installs alongside a system-level Chromium.

--- a/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h
+++ b/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 
 // The brand-specific product name to be included as a component of the install
 // and user data directory paths.
-inline constexpr wchar_t kProductPathName[] = L"Chromium";
+inline constexpr wchar_t kProductPathName[] = L"Excalibur";
 
 // The brand-specific safe browsing client name.
 inline constexpr char kSafeBrowsingName[] = "chromium";
@@ -54,23 +54,23 @@
         .logo_suffix = L"",  // No logo suffix for the primary install mode.
         .app_guid =
             L"",  // Empty app_guid since no integration with Google Update.
-        .base_app_name = L"Chromium",              // A distinct base_app_name.
-        .base_app_id = L"Chromium",                // A distinct base_app_id.
-        .browser_prog_id_prefix = L"ChromiumHTM",  // Browser ProgID prefix.
+        .base_app_name = L"Excalibur",            // A distinct base_app_name.
+        .base_app_id = L"Excalibur",              // A distinct base_app_id.
+        .browser_prog_id_prefix = L"ExcalibHTM",  // Browser ProgID prefix.
         .browser_prog_id_description =
-            L"Chromium HTML Document",  // Browser ProgID description.
-        .direct_launch_url_scheme = "chromium",
-        .pdf_prog_id_prefix = L"ChromiumPDF",  // PDF ProgID prefix.
+            L"Excalibur HTML Document",  // Browser ProgID description.
+        .direct_launch_url_scheme = "excalibur",
+        .pdf_prog_id_prefix = L"ExcalibPDF",  // PDF ProgID prefix.
         .pdf_prog_id_description =
